      "source": {
        "source_id": "bakry-emery-curvature-interpolation:bakry-emery-curvature-interpolation-expression",
        "anchor": "Chewi edition 2026-08-09, Definitions 1.2.28–1.2.29, book pp.18–19 / PDF pp.30–31",
        "url": "https://chewisinho.github.io/main.pdf#page=31",
        "original_text": "Let X be any type, let L be a real-linear operator on real-valued functions on X, and let alpha>0. Assume that for every g:X→R and y:X, alpha Gamma_L(g,g)(y) is at most one half of L(Gamma_L(g,g))(y) minus Gamma_L(g,Lg)(y) minus Gamma_L(g,Lg)(y). Then for every f:X→R and x:X, 2 alpha Gamma_L(f,f)(x) is at most L(Gamma_L(f,f))(x) minus 2 Gamma_L(f,Lf)(x). This is only pointwise real algebra; no semigroup derivative identity is included.",
        "text_sha256": "214f0db8d058ab985735f194cfc0f5cf90af009f4547883e6117b625e03b6792"
      },
      "lean": {
        "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.StochasticProcesses.interpolationDerivative_lower_bound_of_expandedBakryEmery",
        "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/StochasticProcesses/BakryEmeryCalculus.lean",
        "statement": "theorem interpolationDerivative_lower_bound_of_expandedBakryEmery\n    (generator : (X → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (X → ℝ))\n    {alpha : ℝ} (_halpha : 0 < alpha)\n    (hcurvature : ∀ (g : X → ℝ) (y : X),\n      alpha * carreDuChamp generator g g y ≤\n        (2 : ℝ)⁻¹ *\n          (generator (carreDuChamp generator g g) y -\n            carreDuChamp generator g (generator g) y -\n            carreDuChamp generator g (generator g) y))\n    (f : X → ℝ) (x : X) :\n    2 * alpha * carreDuChamp generator f f x ≤\n      generator (carreDuChamp generator f f) x -\n        2 * carreDuChamp generator f (generator f) x",
        "statement_sha256": "ee367d8215ea3fe1de453919d3164dc6bac3cf619c547651978cc11693a72ee7",
